==English==

===Alternative forms===
*[[dilly dally]]
*[[dillydally]]

===Etymology===
Although not recorded as such in the OED, there is phrase in Hindi/Urdu Dhili DhAli or dheely dhaaly, meaning deliberately slowly or, with a modal verb, to procrastinate or waste time. It seems more than likely that this phrase has made its way into the English language from this source rather than from the old French 'dalier' meaning to spend time with one's beloved.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|dilly-dallies|dilly-dallying|dilly-dallied}}
# to [[dawdle]]; to waste time; to [[procrastinate]]

